## Prerequisites

- Kubernetes {{ .KubeVersion }}.
- Gateway API CRDs and a `Gateway` to attach to (`route.parentRef`).
- Prometheus Operator CRDs when `metrics.enabled` is true.
- Two Secrets in the release namespace, each with `DB_HOST`, `DB_PORT`, `DB_USER`, `DB_PASSWORD`
  and `DB_NAME`: `dbSecretName` for the app (DML grants) and `migration.dbSecretName` for the
  migrate hook (DDL grants). `infra/modules/mysql-cluster` creates both.

## Install

```bash
helm upgrade --install posts-api charts/posts-api -n posts-api --set route.hostname=posts.example.test
```

`route.hostname` has no default and the release fails without it. The migrate Job runs on the first
install too: the hook is `pre-install,pre-upgrade`.

## Upgrades

The migrate Job runs before the Deployment changes. A failed Job aborts the upgrade before any
manifest is applied, so the running release stays as it was, and the Job stays in the namespace for
inspection. A Job still running at `activeDeadlineSeconds` (240s) fails the same way.

